{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361769-how-do-you-make-memorable-mortals-for-young-dynasts-to-be-surrounded-by","id":1361769,"title":"How do you make memorable Mortals for young Dynasts to be surrounded by?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-18T10:49:28-08:00","id":1361769,"title":"How do you make memorable Mortals for young Dynasts to be surrounded by?","content":"Inspired by<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361215#post1361215\"> this post,</a> &amp; part 3 followup to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357521-tell-me-about-your-dynasty-s-secondary-schools-games#post1357521\">this thread</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manuel of Exalted Power: The Dragon Blooded, pg18</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dynastic children are handed over to wet nurses within moments of their birth lest they form an inappropriate bond with their mothers. Infancy is spent among young, un-Exalted women of the household and nurses who attend to their every need.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manuel of Exalted Power: The Dragon Blooded, pg19</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Dynastic children are handed over to wet nurses within moments of their birth lest they form an inappropriate bond with their mothers. Infancy is spent among young, un-Exalted women of the household and nurses who attend to their every need.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manuel of Exalted Power: The Dragon Blooded, pg19</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...30 to 40 mortals to take care of the cooking, cleaning, tutoring and secretarial matters. One thing a Dynastic upbringing is not is lonely. Privacy is nearly impossible, and where it is possible, it is usually considered suspicious. Solitude is an unheard-of luxury for the Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>O.K. I'm not going to go this freakin' crazy, but I get the idea of Mortals around young Dynasts is important, there can be a good number of them, &amp; I'd like to make some of them memorable. Nurses. Mentors. Servants. Un-exalted family members.<br /> <br /> I can of course have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361189-poll-what-canon-dynastic-npc-should-be-the-parents-gardians-to-these-pc-s?p=1361400#post1361400\">few magical &amp; special servants</a> (thank you JohnDoe244), but what about the normie-norms that have to round out some of their ranks?<br /> <br /> What would make a few of them stand out to young Dynast PC's?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Do you have some favorite NPC's you've made that you'd like to share? </b></span><br /> <br /> I know you are a creative bunch. <i>Show off your stuff! </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T02:45:33-08:00","id":1361878,"title":"","content":"Well one good way is to just give some of them quirky personalities and little idiosyncrasies. Also remember that as Dynasts they basically have their pick of whatever slaves or servants they want. If they want their child to be tutored in a regional martial art from the South, then they could have the former <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=upcWBut9mrI\" target=\"_blank\">jannisary captain</a> of the royal guard be their teacher for example.<br /> <br /> Something else is that skilled mortals are a big part of the dynasty too. There's thousands and thousands of DBs, but millions of mortals that run it. Reading through the 1e aspect books there's a few notable examples where a Dynast's closest friend and ally is a mortal. Somebody with connections, skills, and dedication could be a great companion as well as asset. You might also have the complete opposite of a world class servant, like for example one who a dynast has a sentimental attachment to a cook who maybe isn't necessarily the best out there at everything he tries to make, but they just can't see it because he was the cook that was with them through the entire northern campaigns cooking for them in the harsh conditions every night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T03:46:21-08:00","id":1361886,"title":"","content":"Played straight, I like Nursey from Blackadder the Third. There's a great mortal in Castebook Air who tells Tepet Arada how it is. I think the most memorable mortals are not exceptional in anything other than having the stones to tell the Dynasts how it is.<br /> <br /> I'm really enjoying Lin in The Fall of Jiara podcasts as well.<br /> <br /> I would farm some of the work onto the players. Have them buy Allies/Retainers/Followers and describe mortals which <b>they</b> find interesting and memorable. Your players don't need to know Exalted to do this -- they describe the character, you tell them how they fit into the game world. No sense coming up with a cast of 30 NPCs who the PCs refuse to interact with.<br /> <br /> But my best advice is just to steal like crazy. You're after rich, privileged humans... who are also servants to demi-god. Pick literally any human character from fiction. Alfred Pennyworth, yes, obviously. But you could also have Bruce Wayne/Batman. And Commissioner Gordon. And even the Joker -- Dynasts run most of the leading crime syndicates. There is no human character from fiction that couldn't be shoehorned into a Dynastic household with a little refluffing. Obvious super-humans... not so much. But heroic mortals? Your retinues can include princes, beggars, assassins, librarians, courtesans and priests. <br /> <br /> Refluff the crew of the Starship Enterprise.<br /> <br /> Major Domo Kirkard <br /> Heads the household's servants but used to travel with the character's parents in their grand tour of the Threshold. Even though it's below his station, he misses his glory days and will try to personally go on missions with the PCs even though he shouldn't really leave the house. Although he's somewhat past his prime, he's a powerfully built brawler who has an affinity with the ladies.<br /> <br /> Maester Syler<br /> Obsessively logical and unemotional, Syler tutors the characters in natural sciences and mechanics. An alchemist, and possibly a sorceror. His pointed ears suggest a fey-blooded heritage, belied by his unemotional nature.<br /> <br /> Feels-The-Bones, a Shaman<br /> Hailing from the distant East, Bones is an aging doctor. Though he speaks Forest tongue and Low Realm he refuses to speak in anything but High Realm. A superb physician, he's quick to remind the Dynasts that his expertise is in human medicine and he refuses to apply his brilliant mind to any other task (&quot;Stitch your clothes? I'm a doctor, not a tailor!&quot;). A sullen and gruff pessimist who makes no secret of his distate for Sylar (&quot;you fey-blooded half-breed.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Power-of-Man, Blacksmith<br /> Hailing from the same village as Bones, Power is a rotund and jolly smith who &quot;gives it all he can, sir&quot;. Speaks with a thick Eastern accent. Secretly a close friend of Bones, the pair often bicker.<br /> <br /> Nyota (Uhura) as scribe and linguist from Harbourhead can be dropped in as is.<br /> <br /> You get the idea. Simply replacing given names with the meaning of those names makes them sound Threshold-y. You don't have to use the Enterprise. Use Voyger with the Federation free being from the character's mother's family, and the Marki being from the father's. Or DS9. Or Babylon 5. Or Farscape. Or Firefly. Or Downton Abby. Or Home and Away. Or the Sweet Life of Cody.<br /> <br /> You can steal from essentially anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-19-2020, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T04:29:08-08:00","id":1361890,"title":"","content":"Mortal NPCs can be an asset because the fairly mundane lives of someone who lived hundreds of years ago can make for an interesting contrast to their little Exalted bubble.<br /> <br /> Like maybe their favourite nanny lost a child and she quietly putting all that energy into nurturing them instead, one of the staff could have been faking literacy for years by simply remembering what lots of different words look like. Obviously avoid taking it to grimdark/dung ages extremes, a little research can go a long way here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}